          "value": "Was initially thought to be a protease involved in deubiquitination because of its similarity with cysteine proteases (PubMed:11090361, PubMed:16301742). However, it was later shown that YopJ is an acetyltransferase that uses a dual substrate mechanism similar to the one used by papain-like proteases (PubMed:16728640)"
